i915: force PWM/AUX-set eDP backlight on Pixel Slate (disable luminance path)

The Google Pixel Slate (nocturne) eDP panel advertises luminance-based
("nits") DPCD backlight control via DP_EDP_PANEL_LUMINANCE_CONTROL_CAPABLE
+ DP_EDP_SMOOTH_BRIGHTNESS_CAPABLE, but does NOT physically honor it: AUX
writes update the sysfs brightness / actual_brightness values but the
panel's actual backlight does not change.

Kernels <= 6.18 drove this panel through the standard AUX/PWM VESA
interface (16-bit pwmgen, max_brightness 65535), which physically works.
Starting in 7.x, i915 selects the luminance-based path for this panel
(max_brightness 7500) and brightness control silently stops working — the
GNOME slider and even direct root writes to
/sys/class/backlight/intel_backlight/brightness no longer dim the panel.

This is BobZKernel's pixel-slate variant, which only ever runs on the
Pixel Slate, so we gate the luminance-control branch off in
intel_dp_aux_supports_vesa_backlight() and fall through to the AUX/PWM
path that physically works. Pair with i915.enable_dpcd_backlight=2
(FORCE_VESA) on the cmdline so the Intel HDR backlight path is skipped too.

Do NOT apply on the other BobZKernel variants — it disables luminance-based
backlight for every eDP panel on the kernel, only desirable where that path
is broken.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c
index 7a6c07f6a..501cbe70c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c
@@ -649,7 +649,8 @@ intel_dp_aux_supports_vesa_backlight(struct intel_connector *connector)
 	struct intel_dp *intel_dp = intel_attached_dp(connector);
 	struct intel_panel *panel = &connector->panel;
 
-	if ((intel_dp->edp_dpcd[3] & DP_EDP_PANEL_LUMINANCE_CONTROL_CAPABLE) &&
+	if (0 && /* BobZKernel pixel-slate: panel lies about luminance ctrl */
+	    (intel_dp->edp_dpcd[3] & DP_EDP_PANEL_LUMINANCE_CONTROL_CAPABLE) &&
 	    (intel_dp->edp_dpcd[3] & DP_EDP_SMOOTH_BRIGHTNESS_CAPABLE)) {
 		drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
 			    "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] AUX Luminance Based Backlight Control Supported!\n",
